1. DERIVED FROM T-ENGINE4 / TALES OF MAJ'EYAL
================================================================================

Inner Datum's simulation engine contains code translated from Lua to TypeScript
from T-Engine4 and the Tales of Maj'Eyal game module.

    T-Engine4 / Tales of Maj'Eyal
    Copyright (C) 2009 - 2018 Nicolas Casalini ("DarkGod")
    <darkgod@te4.org>  -  https://te4.org/  -  https://te4.org/license
    Licensed GPL-3.0-or-later.

Translating a program from one language to another produces a derivative work.
This project is GPL because of that, willingly and gratefully: ToME's combat
model is the reason this game feels the way it does.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1.1  Upstream licence, verified against the source rather than assumed
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  * 1,652 of 1,655.lua files carry the header "either version 3 of the
    License, or (at your option) any later version".
  * The remaining 3 -- game/modules/tome/data/lore/arena.lua,
    game/modules/tome/data/talents/spells/infusion.lua, and
    game/modules/tome/data/zones/keepsake-meadow/zone.lua -- carry no per-file
    header and fall under the project-wide COPYING, which is the verbatim GNU
    General Public License version 3.
  * No file in the tree references GPL version 2.
  * Copyright lines present: "2009 - 2018 Nicolas Casalini" (1,626 files),
    "2009, 2010, 2011, 2012, 2013 Nicolas Casalini" (14),
    "2009 - 2014 Nicolas Casalini" (7).
  * reference/t-engine4/CONTRIBUTING records that contributors assign copyright
    to Nicolas Casalini or grant him relicensing rights, so the grant above is
    made by a single unified rights holder. There is no fragmented-ownership
    risk in the tree we are porting from.

Therefore the correct SPDX identifier is GPL-3.0-or-later. Declaring
GPL-3.0-only would strip a right upstream deliberately granted.

Reference clone used for the port:
    repository:  https://github.com/vgawen/t-engine4.git
    commit:      304327e0805ca3e2ecdd1c8a6ec2e154bee7411e   (2018-09-21)
    location:    reference/t-engine4/ -- read-only, gitignored, never edited.

That commit is the anchor for every `file:line` citation in docs/ and in the
per-file headers under src/. If the clone is recreated at a different commit,
the citations silently shift.

