--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1.3  Files that are NOT derived from T-Engine4
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Written from scratch. Still GPL-3.0-or-later, because they are part of this
program -- but no upstream expression is present in them. Recorded so the
boundary stays legible to anyone auditing the port.

  src/shared/rng.ts                 PCG32. ToME's rng.* is native C and is
                                    absent from the source distribution.
  src/server/engine/fov.ts, los.ts  Shadowcasting. ToME's core.fov is native C
                                    and is absent.
  src/server/engine/barrier.ts      The Bell, quorum, Standing By. No ToME analogue.
  src/server/engine/control.ts      Replaces TOME/class/Player.lua:401-411's
                                    `game.paused` global with per-actor awaited
                                    network commands.
  src/server/world/party.ts         Design referenced from TOME/class/Party.lua;
                                    no code translated.
  src/server/talents/**             Original TypeScript. Balance NUMBERS were
                                    read from TOME/data/talents/**; the
                                    behaviour is ours.
  src/server/{net,http,persist,view,gm,ops,content}/**
  src/client/**
  tools/**, test/**


================================================================================
2. NO TALES OF MAJ'EYAL ART OR AUDIO IS USED
================================================================================

reference/t-engine4/COPYING-MEDIA states, in full:

    All the medias located in all the "/data/gfx" folders are granted to use
    with the Tales of Maj'Eyal game only.

    Please contact darkgod@te4.org for more informations.

No file from any ToME media directory appears in this repository. The exclusion
is satisfied by construction, not by discipline, and now by two independent
mechanisms:

  1. The reference clone is sparse and never fetches those paths at all, so
     there is no local copy to reproduce from. It is retained for source
     consultation only, and is gitignored.
  2. NO MEDIA OF ANY KIND IS TRACKED IN THIS REPOSITORY. The art tree is
     excluded wholesale (see ASSETS-LICENSE.md), so there is no tracked
     directory for a media file to be committed into -- ToME's or anyone
     else's.

Copy code logic only, and cite it when you do.


